pullen@pratt.cs.washington.edu (Walter D. Pullen) writes:

>I remember that there were a few postings a while back detailing a way
>that one could remove items from a shop without setting off the alarm,

There are several ways. Wands/portions/spells/whatever for digging
and teleportation are very handy. Also, if you have a wand of sleep
you can use it on the shopkeeper when he steps away from the door
(sometimes he walks a little bit around while you're at the farthest
ends of the shop). Wands of death come in handy also - they're one
of the few things that effectively and clean does away with
the shopkeeper.

When I enter a shop, I usually pick up all the stuff that I want
regardsless of whether I can pay it or not (rather anti-social
attitude but..). If I don't have any known practical spells or wands,
I simply start trying first all the wands, then the spellbooks,
then quaffing all the potions - until I find something that works. You
may find wands etc. in the shop itself that will get you out of it.

Hmm, what else. Yes! You should of course also try any scrolls that you
find. Also, when you test unknown wands, don't point them at the
shopkeeper until you know what they do (he's pretty easy to upset) -
also stand well away from the walls in case a wand bounces.

Before attempting to get out of the shop, make sure that you have
a reasonable amounts of hitpoints (Hp). If you succeed, you're
going to have a lot of keystone kops after you. They're pretty
easy to kill, but since there are so many, you can quickly die
if you're low on hp's.

Thats about what I can remember at the moment.

